1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Are you a moviegoer?
你是一名影迷吗？

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:11,310
If, like me, you’re a fan of film, then there’s no better place to watch something than on the big screen at the cinema.
如果你和我一样热爱电影，那么没有什么地方比电影院的大屏幕更适合观影了。

3
00:00:11,310 --> 00:00:17,910
You enter the dark auditorium and take your seat, ready to be entertained.
你走进昏暗的放映厅，落座之后，便准备好开启一场视听盛宴。

4
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:26,210
But while you engross yourself in some movie magic, many others are now getting their film fix at home.
但就在你沉浸于电影的奇幻魅力时，如今有许多人选择在家就能过足电影瘾。

5
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:31,380
Over the last few years, cinemas have seen a resurgence.
在过去几年里，电影院行业迎来了复苏。

6
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:39,820
Customers have been enticed by comfortable seats, and lots of choice of things to watch.
舒适的座椅以及丰富多样的影片选择，吸引了不少观众前来。

7
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:49,470
Multiplexes in particular can screen up to twenty films at the same time, catering for all different tastes.
尤其是多厅影院，能够同时放映多达二十部影片，满足不同观众的口味。

8
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:57,660
In addition, 3D and even 4D movies can give the audience an extra immersive experience.
此外，3D甚至4D电影还能为观众带来更具沉浸感的体验。

9
00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:02,070
So, what’s not to like about a trip to the cinema?
如此说来，去电影院观影还有什么让人不满意的地方呢？

10
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:06,240
One answer to that question is convenience.
这个问题的答案之一就是便利性。

11
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:20,720
Rather than going out, it’s so much easier to stay in and watch a romcom or action movie on a high-definition TV screen via a streaming service such as Netflix or Amazon Prime.
比起出门，待在家里通过网飞或亚马逊Prime这类流媒体平台，在高清电视屏幕上看一部浪漫喜剧或动作片要轻松得多。

12
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:25,640
There’s plenty of choice, and it’s relatively cheap as well.
影片选择十分丰富，价格也相对实惠。

13
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:33,220
But, personally, I find there are too many distractions, and watching at home is not such an event.
但就我个人而言，我觉得在家观影干扰太多，和影院观影完全不是一回事。

14
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,870
I miss the trailers too!
我还很想念电影预告片呢！

15
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:42,040
But the coronavirus pandemic has put the future of cinemas under the spotlight.
但新冠疫情的爆发让电影院的未来被推上了风口浪尖。

16
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:46,040
Some have had to close because of reduced ticket sales.
部分影院因票房收入下滑而不得不关门歇业。

17
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:54,940
And in the UK, it’s brought about a surge in TV watching and online streaming, according to media watchdog, Ofcom.
英国媒体监管机构英国通信管理局表示，疫情还使得英国的电视观看量和在线流媒体播放量大幅飙升。

18
00:01:54,940 --> 00:02:03,140
It also found that half of UK adults will keep and continue using their new streaming subscriptions.
该机构还发现，有一半的英国成年人会保留并继续使用他们新订阅的流媒体服务。

19
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,410
This isn’t great news for cinemas.
这对电影院来说绝非好消息。

20
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:18,370
They rely on the release of a big blockbuster to bring the crowds back, but the launch of new films, such as James Bond: No Time To Die, are being delayed.
它们本指望依靠一部重磅大片的上映来吸引观众回流，但《007：无暇赴死》等新片的上映计划却纷纷被推迟。

21
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:26,560
And Disney has released its $200m blockbuster, Mulan, online instead of in movie theatres.
迪士尼更是将其耗资2亿美元打造的大片《花木兰》选择在线上发行，而非在影院上映。

22
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:41,110
But John Fithian, from the National Association of Theatre Owners, told Variety magazine: “This idea of waiting out the pandemic to make your movies more profitable doesn’t make sense to me.
不过，美国影院业主协会的约翰·菲西安在接受《综艺》杂志采访时表示：“这种想着熬过疫情再让电影赚更多钱的想法，在我看来毫无道理。

23
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:46,500
There won’t be as much of an industry left to play your movies in if you do that.”
如果真这么做，到时候这个行业恐怕就剩不下多少能放映你们影片的影院了。”
